1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:04,379
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:10,927 --> 00:00:15,765
<i>Only I have the right</i>
<i>to discipline Arnaldo.</i>

3
00:00:15,849 --> 00:00:17,100
<i>But how did he turn out?!</i>

4
00:00:17,183 --> 00:00:19,227
<i>He's no different than you!</i>
<i>He's a criminal now!</i>

5
00:00:19,310 --> 00:00:22,105
<i>-Kill this insolent bastard!</i>
<i>-Papa! Papa, don't!</i>

6
00:00:22,188 --> 00:00:23,940
<i>Get out of here, Raul. Leave.</i>

7
00:00:24,023 --> 00:00:26,901
[Arnaldo] <i>I haven't killed</i>
<i>anyone aside from Nimfa.</i>

8
00:00:26,985 --> 00:00:29,070
<i>Wait, if you release this, that means…</i>

9
00:00:29,154 --> 00:00:32,365
<i>That's the only way</i>
<i>I can think of to help Diego</i>

10
00:00:32,449 --> 00:00:34,701
<i>and put a stop to Arnaldo's ruthlessness.</i>

11
00:00:34,784 --> 00:00:37,412
<i>Lily's coming back,</i>
<i>so they better watch out.</i>

12
00:00:37,495 --> 00:00:39,497
<i>I feel Ivy is keeping</i>
<i>her true relationship</i>

13
00:00:39,581 --> 00:00:40,707
<i>with Diego a secret.</i>

14
00:00:40,790 --> 00:00:42,292
<i>Test her. Use Diego.</i>

15
00:00:45,128 --> 00:00:46,588
[Diego] <i>Fight me fair and square.</i>

16
00:00:46,671 --> 00:00:48,673
[Arnaldo] <i>Fight? I'm finishing</i>
<i>you off right here.</i>

17
00:00:48,757 --> 00:00:50,884
[Arnaldo grunts]

18
00:00:50,967 --> 00:00:52,218
<i>Diego! Stop it!</i>

19
00:00:52,302 --> 00:00:53,928
<i>This isn't over.</i>

20
00:00:54,012 --> 00:00:57,265
<i>I'd like to propose something.</i>
<i>Let's do a pre-election survey.</i>

21
00:00:57,348 --> 00:00:59,601
<i>Whoever wins there is the one</i>
<i>who's telling the truth.</i>

22
00:00:59,684 --> 00:01:00,894
<i>Now, who are they going to choose?</i>

23
00:01:00,977 --> 00:01:03,980
<i>A criminal,</i>
<i>or an honest politician like me?</i>

24
00:01:04,064 --> 00:01:05,065
<i>Let them decide.</i>

25
00:01:05,148 --> 00:01:06,566
[Raul] <i>Gather all our men.</i>

26
00:01:06,649 --> 00:01:09,235
<i>And round up every judge in Ardiente.</i>

27
00:01:09,319 --> 00:01:12,155
<i>I am not going to reshape</i>
<i>Ardiente. You are.</i>

28
00:01:12,238 --> 00:01:14,741
<i>If you really love our province,</i>
<i>you'll choose what is right.</i>

29
00:01:14,824 --> 00:01:16,701
<i>You will choose change.</i>

30
00:01:16,785 --> 00:01:19,037
[Natalie] <i>Who did Emilia ask you to find?</i>

31
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:20,663
<i>Miss Lily Cruz.</i>

32
00:01:21,331 --> 00:01:23,083
<i>Lily Cruz, huh?</i>

33
00:01:23,166 --> 00:01:24,250
<i>That's impossible!</i>

34
00:01:24,334 --> 00:01:26,419
<i>Diego beat me?! I don't believe it!</i>

35
00:01:26,878 --> 00:01:29,464
<i>How did this dog beat you?!</i>

36
00:01:30,590 --> 00:01:31,591
<i>Well?</i>

37
00:01:35,595 --> 00:01:36,513
Auntie.

38
00:01:36,596 --> 00:01:37,764
-[Camia] Diego.
-Attorney.

39
00:01:40,850 --> 00:01:42,018
DIEGO TORILLO SECURES
LANDSLIDE SURVEY WIN

40
00:01:43,937 --> 00:01:44,854
[Camia chuckles]

41
00:01:44,938 --> 00:01:46,856
Diego, you got 82%!

42
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:51,027
That means the people
of Ardiente have faith in you!

43
00:01:51,111 --> 00:01:52,487
That's why, as early as now,

44
00:01:52,570 --> 00:01:55,073
I'm confident you're going to
win the election.

45
00:01:55,156 --> 00:01:56,866
-Auntie!
-[Camia chuckles]

46
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:58,243
And I have another good news for you.

47
00:01:58,326 --> 00:02:01,788
-Sit down, please.
-Judge De Jesus is back…

48
00:02:01,871 --> 00:02:03,414
And she withdrew from your case.

49
00:02:03,998 --> 00:02:06,126
A new judge is handling this now.

50
00:02:06,209 --> 00:02:08,461
It's Judge Rotico
from the neighboring province.

51
00:02:08,545 --> 00:02:11,256
We've got a high chance
of winning this case, Diego.

52
00:02:12,090 --> 00:02:13,091
[Camia] Diego.

53
00:02:14,592 --> 00:02:15,760
[Camia] Thank you, Attorney.

54
00:02:15,844 --> 00:02:17,679
Thank you so much, Attorney!

55
00:02:18,763 --> 00:02:21,141
[tense music playing]

56
00:02:27,313 --> 00:02:28,731
DIEGO TORILLO SECURES
LANDSLIDE SURVEY WIN

57
00:02:28,815 --> 00:02:30,066
[Raul] Rufo!

58
00:02:32,068 --> 00:02:33,319
Yes, Jaguar?

59
00:02:34,362 --> 00:02:36,906
Have our men guard Diego in jail.

60
00:02:38,032 --> 00:02:40,535
I'm sure the Ardientes aren't happy

61
00:02:41,494 --> 00:02:43,413
about the results of the survey.

62
00:02:43,496 --> 00:02:44,998
I'll get right to it, Jaguar.

63
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:48,126
If things get out of hand,
you know what to do.

64
00:02:49,502 --> 00:02:50,795
Break Diego out…

65
00:02:52,213 --> 00:02:53,381
and bring him here.

66
00:02:55,717 --> 00:02:57,385
[tense music playing]

67
00:03:00,847 --> 00:03:02,765
This sucks!

68
00:03:03,308 --> 00:03:05,476
[frustrated] Eighty-two percent?!

69
00:03:06,728 --> 00:03:08,646
That's a humongous number!

70
00:03:08,730 --> 00:03:13,776
That basically ensures Diego's
victory in this election!

71
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:16,738
No! That's not gonna happen!
I'm going to win.

72
00:03:17,572 --> 00:03:19,574
-Me!
-Of course, you are.

73
00:03:19,657 --> 00:03:23,953
We Ardientes are the rightful
leaders of this town.

74
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:26,581
That is why…

75
00:03:27,832 --> 00:03:31,127
we're going to have Diego killed.

76
00:03:31,544 --> 00:03:33,129
[tense music playing]

77
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:36,341
Hello.

78
00:03:37,217 --> 00:03:39,928
Finish off Diego Torillo.

79
00:03:47,352 --> 00:03:48,353
Done.

80
00:03:54,734 --> 00:03:57,737
[ominous music playing]

81
00:04:03,868 --> 00:04:05,119
[jail cell opening]

82
00:04:07,372 --> 00:04:10,917
[sinister music playing]

83
00:04:20,718 --> 00:04:22,387
[action music playing]

84
00:04:26,057 --> 00:04:27,141
[goon shouts]

85
00:04:44,158 --> 00:04:46,911
[tense music playing]

86
00:04:53,167 --> 00:04:54,836
[screams in pain]

87
00:05:02,302 --> 00:05:04,095
-Think you're so tough?!
-Fight back!

88
00:05:04,178 --> 00:05:05,888
[goon shouting] Show us what you got!

89
00:05:07,348 --> 00:05:08,516
[goon laughing]

90
00:05:08,599 --> 00:05:10,476
Fight back! Get up!

91
00:05:12,687 --> 00:05:13,521
Get him!

92
00:05:27,493 --> 00:05:29,454
[action music playing]

93
00:05:29,537 --> 00:05:31,331
[goon] You got spunk! Get up!

94
00:05:37,837 --> 00:05:39,047
[goon cackling]

95
00:05:39,672 --> 00:05:41,466
What now? Kneel!

96
00:05:43,092 --> 00:05:44,886
-[laughter]
-I said kneel!

97
00:05:45,595 --> 00:05:47,972
-Come on! Get up!
-Get up!

98
00:05:48,973 --> 00:05:51,309
-Stubborn, eh?
-You aren't so tough now!

99
00:05:55,646 --> 00:05:57,190
[grunting]

100
00:05:57,940 --> 00:06:00,193
[goons cackling]

101
00:06:00,276 --> 00:06:01,360
[goons jeering]

102
00:06:01,444 --> 00:06:02,445
What?!

103
00:06:05,531 --> 00:06:06,866
Going to fight back?

104
00:06:07,366 --> 00:06:09,452
[tense music playing]

105
00:06:09,535 --> 00:06:10,536
[goon] More!

106
00:06:11,037 --> 00:06:12,580
[goon cackling]

107
00:06:16,459 --> 00:06:17,710
So, what's it going to be?

108
00:06:19,128 --> 00:06:20,379
[goon laughing]

109
00:06:29,639 --> 00:06:30,973
I thought he was tough.

110
00:06:32,475 --> 00:06:33,726
Why don't you cry?

111
00:06:33,810 --> 00:06:35,019
So?

112
00:06:35,103 --> 00:06:38,856
Dude, finish him. Congressman's orders.

113
00:06:40,149 --> 00:06:41,818
[tense music playing]

114
00:06:48,533 --> 00:06:50,785
Ivy, where are you going?

115
00:06:51,285 --> 00:06:53,955
Oh, just some matters to attend to. Work.

116
00:06:54,956 --> 00:06:57,250
Would you rather put work first

117
00:06:57,333 --> 00:06:58,960
than console my son on his defeat?

118
00:07:00,211 --> 00:07:04,340
Well, Emilia, I already spoke
to Arnaldo. He understands me.

119
00:07:04,757 --> 00:07:07,385
And I'm sure you know
how important work is.

120
00:07:07,468 --> 00:07:08,469
[Emilia sighs]

121
00:07:09,053 --> 00:07:10,430
Yes, you're right, Ivy.

122
00:07:11,806 --> 00:07:13,307
But why don't you come with me?

123
00:07:14,725 --> 00:07:16,769
Why don't you accompany me?

124
00:07:17,979 --> 00:07:21,107
Whatever it is, I'm sorry,
I'm not interested.

125
00:07:21,816 --> 00:07:22,859
Are you sure?

126
00:07:23,776 --> 00:07:26,696
Even if it's about Lily Cruz?

127
00:07:32,618 --> 00:07:33,828
You see, Ivy…

128
00:07:33,911 --> 00:07:36,289
I've long been looking for Lily Cruz.

129
00:07:36,956 --> 00:07:41,210
All my hard work paid off!
I'll finally meet her.

130
00:07:41,586 --> 00:07:43,546
And I also want you to meet her.

131
00:07:44,088 --> 00:07:44,922
You know,

132
00:07:45,006 --> 00:07:47,842
you might have a lot of things
in common with each other.

133
00:07:56,476 --> 00:07:58,269
Congrats! Finally!

134
00:07:59,061 --> 00:08:01,772
You'll finally meet Lily Cruz!

135
00:08:02,273 --> 00:08:04,775
The person Emilia fears the most.

136
00:08:05,693 --> 00:08:08,488
-Me? Afraid of Lily Cruz?
-Yes!

137
00:08:08,571 --> 00:08:10,865
Don't you remember? You passed out.

138
00:08:11,282 --> 00:08:12,825
But don't worry, future mother-in-law.

139
00:08:12,909 --> 00:08:16,120
I always carry some ammonia
in case you pass out again.

140
00:08:16,454 --> 00:08:17,830
[both giggling]

141
00:08:17,914 --> 00:08:21,042
You know, Ivy, we really love
mocking each other, right?

142
00:08:21,667 --> 00:08:24,128
[sighs] But you see,
I want you to come along

143
00:08:24,212 --> 00:08:29,050
because I want you to witness
how I become a ruthless bitch.

144
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:31,886
Because this time,

145
00:08:32,762 --> 00:08:34,013
I will…

146
00:08:36,807 --> 00:08:39,393
kill Lily Cruz myself.

147
00:08:40,770 --> 00:08:43,314
Bang! Bang! Bang!

148
00:08:43,397 --> 00:08:44,524
[laughs]

149
00:08:44,607 --> 00:08:45,399
Three!

150
00:08:45,483 --> 00:08:48,611
Straight in the heart! It's like saying…

151
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:53,324
"Die, bitch! Die, bitch!
I hate you, bitch!"

152
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:58,371
Hey. Are you scared? You look pale.

153
00:08:59,372 --> 00:09:02,875
It's as if you're saying
that you're Lily Cruz!

154
00:09:02,959 --> 00:09:06,337
Oh, Ivy. Didn't I tell you?

155
00:09:07,171 --> 00:09:08,422
I got your back.

156
00:09:09,173 --> 00:09:11,300
Chill! Relax.

157
00:09:12,593 --> 00:09:14,136
The end is near.

158
00:09:15,638 --> 00:09:16,639
Come!

159
00:09:16,722 --> 00:09:18,599
[tense music playing]

160
00:09:30,152 --> 00:09:31,821
You want to chill?

161
00:09:36,075 --> 00:09:37,326
I'll help you.

162
00:09:39,036 --> 00:09:40,913
[goon] Dude, finish him.

163
00:09:44,041 --> 00:09:46,544
[tense music playing]

164
00:09:48,504 --> 00:09:50,464
[goon shouting]

165
00:09:53,884 --> 00:09:55,219
[Diego screaming in pain]

166
00:09:55,803 --> 00:09:57,013
[goons laughing]

167
00:09:57,096 --> 00:09:58,014
You got him!

168
00:09:59,807 --> 00:10:01,183
[goons jeering]

169
00:10:02,143 --> 00:10:03,477
He's a bastard.

170
00:10:11,527 --> 00:10:13,195
[tense music playing]

171
00:10:16,115 --> 00:10:18,326
Don't try anything else on my son…

172
00:10:19,285 --> 00:10:21,329
or I'll kill you, Julio Ardiente.

173
00:10:23,456 --> 00:10:26,208
[action music playing]

174
00:10:38,929 --> 00:10:39,930
Hey!

175
00:10:41,599 --> 00:10:42,600
Get away from him.

176
00:10:45,394 --> 00:10:46,479
[man shouting]

177
00:11:03,788 --> 00:11:04,747
Diego!

178
00:11:07,124 --> 00:11:08,376
Let's get out of here!

179
00:11:09,001 --> 00:11:10,002
Come on!

180
00:11:10,795 --> 00:11:11,879
Come on!

181
00:11:11,962 --> 00:11:12,838
[Diego] Wait! Wait!

182
00:11:12,922 --> 00:11:14,298
Come on! Come on!

183
00:11:14,382 --> 00:11:15,216
No! Who are you?

184
00:11:15,299 --> 00:11:16,967
We're Jaguar's men. Let's go!

185
00:11:17,885 --> 00:11:19,595
-Who's Jaguar?
-Let's go! Let's go!

186
00:11:19,678 --> 00:11:21,889
-Who's Jaguar?!
-You'll find out soon enough.

187
00:11:21,972 --> 00:11:22,890
Let's go!

188
00:11:22,973 --> 00:11:24,809
Diego, you're going to die
if you stay here!

189
00:11:24,892 --> 00:11:26,185
Do you understand?! Come on!

190
00:11:26,685 --> 00:11:27,436
Let's go.

191
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:30,022
I don't care! I'm not going with you!

192
00:11:34,443 --> 00:11:35,611
You really are stubborn.

193
00:11:36,028 --> 00:11:37,196
Jaguar was right.

194
00:11:39,782 --> 00:11:40,658
Let's go, Diego! Come on!

195
00:11:40,741 --> 00:11:43,452
-I'm not going with you!
-Quit it! Come with us!

196
00:11:43,536 --> 00:11:45,079
-I don't need to escape!
-Hurry!

197
00:11:45,162 --> 00:11:47,540
-I'm innocent!
-Come with us! Hurry!

198
00:11:47,623 --> 00:11:49,291
I'm not going with you!

199
00:11:51,669 --> 00:11:53,087
Come on! Let's get out of here!

200
00:11:54,088 --> 00:11:56,924
Wait. Wait! Who's Jaguar?!

201
00:11:58,008 --> 00:11:59,009
Wait!

202
00:11:59,093 --> 00:12:01,345
[action music continues]

203
00:12:09,311 --> 00:12:10,396
Over here!

204
00:12:12,106 --> 00:12:13,107
Get them up.

205
00:12:13,190 --> 00:12:14,191
Come on!

206
00:12:15,359 --> 00:12:17,736
Get up! Get up!

207
00:12:18,779 --> 00:12:21,073
-[Diego] Wait, I'm injured.
-Get up!

208
00:12:21,157 --> 00:12:22,741
-Take him.
-Wait.

209
00:12:23,451 --> 00:12:24,577
Go on. Hurry.

210
00:12:30,332 --> 00:12:32,543
Finally, it's over.

211
00:12:33,919 --> 00:12:35,337
Diego is done for.

212
00:12:37,214 --> 00:12:38,257
My problem is solved.

213
00:12:39,049 --> 00:12:42,803
<i>Our</i> problem, Grandpa.
No one can block my candidacy.

214
00:12:42,887 --> 00:12:45,681
And the result
of the survey? It's useless.

215
00:12:45,764 --> 00:12:46,891
Good as null and void.

216
00:12:47,308 --> 00:12:51,312
On top of that, no one can
bother me and Ivy anymore.

217
00:12:51,854 --> 00:12:56,609
Well, a fitting fairy-tale ending
for both of you.

218
00:12:57,026 --> 00:13:00,613
That's why we deserve
this prime rib that we're partaking.

219
00:13:00,696 --> 00:13:02,281
-Eat up, boy.
-That's right.

220
00:13:02,823 --> 00:13:05,326
Oh, by the way, Grandpa, I'm just curious

221
00:13:05,409 --> 00:13:08,078
because I've been meaning to ask you
this for a long time already.

222
00:13:08,162 --> 00:13:09,997
Why did you even raise Diego?

223
00:13:10,873 --> 00:13:14,168
Come on, you sent him to school
and gave him the name Ardiente.

224
00:13:14,251 --> 00:13:16,587
He was already a bad investment
from the start

225
00:13:16,670 --> 00:13:18,714
since you knew he was
my dad's illegitimate child.

226
00:13:20,007 --> 00:13:22,176
It was all because of your mother.

227
00:13:23,260 --> 00:13:26,388
Your mother and her blind,

228
00:13:26,472 --> 00:13:31,310
dumb, stupid love for your father, Raul.

229
00:13:33,395 --> 00:13:35,689
Okay, that made sense.

230
00:13:35,773 --> 00:13:39,318
What if Dad brainwashes Mom again…

231
00:13:39,401 --> 00:13:42,029
and asks her to have Diego released?

232
00:13:42,112 --> 00:13:43,739
That would be too late…

233
00:13:43,822 --> 00:13:47,826
because even as we're
having dinner and speaking,

234
00:13:48,494 --> 00:13:50,829
Diego may be taking in his last breath.

235
00:13:52,414 --> 00:13:53,707
[Julio chuckles]

236
00:13:55,584 --> 00:14:00,798
Here's to your victory
as the future leader

237
00:14:00,881 --> 00:14:02,383
of the Ardiente clan.

238
00:14:03,509 --> 00:14:04,510
Cheers to that.

239
00:14:15,521 --> 00:14:16,480
[moans]

240
00:14:16,564 --> 00:14:20,025
[bleak music playing]

241
00:14:21,694 --> 00:14:23,112
Are you sure she's here?

242
00:14:23,195 --> 00:14:25,114
Yes, ma'am. Let's go inside.

243
00:14:26,907 --> 00:14:28,993
Emilia, wait.

244
00:14:30,619 --> 00:14:31,745
This feels off.

245
00:14:33,831 --> 00:14:34,874
[sighs]

246
00:14:35,457 --> 00:14:39,545
I have a bad feeling about this.
Let's go home.

247
00:14:39,628 --> 00:14:42,172
Oh, come on! It's too late to back out.

248
00:14:42,256 --> 00:14:45,509
Don't be a party pooper!
Lily's waiting. Hurry up.

249
00:14:45,593 --> 00:14:48,762
No! We have to go home. Let's go.

250
00:14:48,846 --> 00:14:51,515
We won't. You will come with me inside…

251
00:14:51,849 --> 00:14:54,268
because I'll use you as a human shield,

252
00:14:54,351 --> 00:14:56,979
just in case Lily Cruz has a gun.

253
00:14:57,771 --> 00:14:59,565
Let's get going. Let's go in.

254
00:14:59,648 --> 00:15:02,818
-Emilia, listen to me!
-Come on, we're here already.

255
00:15:02,902 --> 00:15:03,861
Hurry up.

256
00:15:03,944 --> 00:15:05,571
[ominous music playing]

257
00:15:08,073 --> 00:15:08,908
Lily!

258
00:15:10,367 --> 00:15:11,952
Lily Cruz!

259
00:15:13,037 --> 00:15:15,581
Lily Cruz, where are you?

260
00:15:16,457 --> 00:15:17,499
Emilia, let's go.

261
00:15:18,083 --> 00:15:21,962
To be honest, I don't trust that
private investigator of yours.

262
00:15:22,755 --> 00:15:23,839
Can you just shut up?

263
00:15:25,215 --> 00:15:29,219
Lily Cruz! Where are you?
I'm getting impatient!

264
00:15:29,678 --> 00:15:33,265
I have something for you! A coffin!

265
00:15:33,933 --> 00:15:35,643
Aren't you excited?

266
00:15:36,060 --> 00:15:38,020
[frustrated] Lily Cruz! Show yourself!

267
00:15:39,146 --> 00:15:40,773
I can't wait any longer!

268
00:15:40,856 --> 00:15:43,317
You're getting on my nerves!

269
00:15:44,109 --> 00:15:45,110
Lily!

270
00:15:46,946 --> 00:15:48,572
[suspenseful music playing]

271
00:15:54,536 --> 00:15:56,997
[hushed tone] Emilia. I told you.

272
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:01,377
[suspenseful music playing]

273
00:16:15,516 --> 00:16:17,184
[suspenseful music playing]

274
00:16:28,153 --> 00:16:30,864
[suspenseful music playing]

275
00:16:36,495 --> 00:16:38,414
[gunshots]

276
00:16:38,497 --> 00:16:39,540
[bullets buzzing]

277
00:16:40,833 --> 00:16:41,834
[Emilia screams]

278
00:16:42,418 --> 00:16:43,460
Emilia, hide!

279
00:16:43,794 --> 00:16:44,795
[Ivy grunts]

280
00:16:45,963 --> 00:16:47,673
[suspenseful music playing]

281
00:16:50,801 --> 00:16:52,886
I told you, Emilia! I told you!

282
00:16:56,849 --> 00:16:57,850
[groans]

283
00:17:00,519 --> 00:17:02,187
If you only listened to me!

284
00:17:04,857 --> 00:17:07,568
[sinister music playing]

285
00:17:17,286 --> 00:17:20,205
[sinister music playing]

286
00:17:33,469 --> 00:17:34,887
[laughing]

287
00:17:37,681 --> 00:17:38,599
Natalie?!

288
00:17:40,059 --> 00:17:42,686
[exhales] Did you pee
in your pants, Emilia?

289
00:17:43,437 --> 00:17:45,147
[Natalie laughing]

290
00:17:45,230 --> 00:17:47,566
Yes! It's me!

291
00:17:48,067 --> 00:17:52,613
And I'm back… in the flesh!

292
00:17:54,114 --> 00:17:57,076
[tense music playing]

293
00:17:59,787 --> 00:18:01,538
You're Lily Cruz?!

294
00:18:01,622 --> 00:18:02,956
[Natalie laughing]

295
00:18:03,624 --> 00:18:04,792
Lily who?!

296
00:18:05,959 --> 00:18:07,002
I don't know who that is.

297
00:18:07,795 --> 00:18:13,092
I just took advantage
of your obsession with finding her

298
00:18:13,759 --> 00:18:18,931
because I'm dying to see you.

299
00:18:20,057 --> 00:18:21,600
[Natalie chuckles]

300
00:18:21,683 --> 00:18:27,856
And I didn't expect that woman
to be here tonight too.

301
00:18:29,149 --> 00:18:36,073
Miss Ivy "Snake" Aguas.

302
00:18:37,241 --> 00:18:41,120
The bitch who stole
the love of my life, Arnaldo.

303
00:18:44,790 --> 00:18:47,251
[laughing]

304
00:18:49,044 --> 00:18:50,671
As far as I'm concerned,

305
00:18:50,963 --> 00:18:53,257
you and Arnaldo are over, Natalie.

306
00:18:53,340 --> 00:18:54,550
I know, right?!

307
00:18:55,384 --> 00:18:57,594
[sighs] My goodness, finally!

308
00:18:58,387 --> 00:19:03,142
But, you and me? We aren't done yet.

309
00:19:03,642 --> 00:19:05,519
You go to hell, you bitch!

310
00:19:05,602 --> 00:19:06,770
Oops!

311
00:19:10,149 --> 00:19:12,860
I'll see you there!

312
00:19:14,736 --> 00:19:16,530
What's your problem, Natalie?

313
00:19:17,322 --> 00:19:20,367
My poor daddy!

314
00:19:22,327 --> 00:19:23,704
He trusted you!

315
00:19:26,415 --> 00:19:28,625
But you had him murdered!

316
00:19:29,001 --> 00:19:30,794
[Natalie breathing heavily]

317
00:19:32,713 --> 00:19:33,881
That's why I'm here.

318
00:19:34,798 --> 00:19:37,384
Because it's payback time, Emilia!

319
00:19:37,467 --> 00:19:39,219
[tense music playing]

320
00:19:39,303 --> 00:19:43,891
I'm going to make you suffer
before you die.

321
00:19:45,225 --> 00:19:46,894
[tense music playing]

322
00:19:50,522 --> 00:19:51,607
[gunshot]

323
00:19:51,690 --> 00:19:53,275
-[Emilia exclaims]
-Emilia!

324
00:19:55,068 --> 00:19:56,904
Split them up!

325
00:19:57,779 --> 00:19:59,865
I'll deal with these bitches separately.

326
00:19:59,948 --> 00:20:02,492
[Emilia] No! Don't do this, Natalie!

327
00:20:02,576 --> 00:20:04,036
If you want to kill someone, kill her!

328
00:20:04,119 --> 00:20:06,580
Kill her, and I promise you…

329
00:20:06,663 --> 00:20:08,749
-Oh.
-you'll have Arnaldo back!

330
00:20:08,832 --> 00:20:12,586
-Seriously, Emilia? Wow!
-[Natalie laughs]

331
00:20:14,129 --> 00:20:15,339
[Natalie sighs]

332
00:20:15,672 --> 00:20:18,717
Emilia, I've finally moved on.

333
00:20:20,636 --> 00:20:26,433
And you might lose it when
I tell you who my new man is!

334
00:20:27,142 --> 00:20:28,810
[tense music playing]

335
00:20:29,353 --> 00:20:30,979
[Natalie laughs hysterically]

336
00:20:31,521 --> 00:20:32,606
[whoops]

337
00:20:32,689 --> 00:20:34,608
-[laughing]
-[goons] Let's go!

338
00:20:34,691 --> 00:20:35,692
-Let's go!
-Let's go!

339
00:20:35,776 --> 00:20:37,319
-Move!
-Don't touch me! Let go!

340
00:20:38,070 --> 00:20:39,029
Don't touch me!

341
00:20:39,112 --> 00:20:40,572
-[goon] Stop resisting.
-What the--

342
00:20:42,074 --> 00:20:44,243
-Ouch!
-[Julio] <i>I wonder…</i>

343
00:20:44,326 --> 00:20:47,037
where your mother and Ivy could be.

344
00:20:49,122 --> 00:20:51,291
Ivy didn't tell me
where they were going either.

345
00:20:52,251 --> 00:20:53,126
As a matter of fact,

346
00:20:53,210 --> 00:20:55,128
she hasn't replied
to any of my text messages.

347
00:20:55,504 --> 00:20:57,172
[ominous music playing]

348
00:20:58,298 --> 00:20:59,675
It's either of two things.

349
00:21:01,176 --> 00:21:02,469
They went out shopping,

350
00:21:03,345 --> 00:21:07,099
or they've done something
foolish like kill each other.

351
00:21:08,016 --> 00:21:12,771
You know, I used to find it
amusing, but not anymore.

352
00:21:14,064 --> 00:21:17,234
Don't say that, Grandpa.
I want them to get along, okay?

353
00:21:17,317 --> 00:21:18,402
[Julio chuckles]

354
00:21:20,570 --> 00:21:23,198
Never! That's never going
to happen, Arnaldo.

355
00:21:24,199 --> 00:21:27,911
You put two bullies in one room,

356
00:21:29,204 --> 00:21:30,789
and there's going to be bloodshed.

357
00:21:31,915 --> 00:21:33,667
Come to think of it, you know,

358
00:21:34,376 --> 00:21:38,922
you were better off
with that Natalie woman.

359
00:21:39,006 --> 00:21:40,007
[Arnaldo scoffs]

360
00:21:40,090 --> 00:21:42,592
At least, she and your mother got along.

361
00:21:44,886 --> 00:21:49,266
If only Emilia hadn't had Pablo killed.

362
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:53,437
Things would've been a lot easier for us.

363
00:21:54,271 --> 00:21:56,773
Well, good thing I don't like it easy.

364
00:21:56,857 --> 00:21:59,735
Okay? I like Ivy because
she challenges me.

365
00:22:01,987 --> 00:22:03,822
She weakens you!

366
00:22:04,406 --> 00:22:06,575
You factor her into
every decision you make!

367
00:22:07,117 --> 00:22:08,327
Do I really have to say it again?

368
00:22:08,410 --> 00:22:12,247
I love her, okay? I love her.
Plain and simple.

369
00:22:12,748 --> 00:22:15,584
And how about Ivy?
Does she truly love you?

370
00:22:17,336 --> 00:22:18,378
Huh?

371
00:22:18,462 --> 00:22:20,088
[tense music playing]

372
00:22:20,714 --> 00:22:24,301
-She does. I know she loves me.
-[scoffs]

373
00:22:24,843 --> 00:22:28,972
Well, well, well… We'll see.

374
00:22:29,598 --> 00:22:35,479
Let's see how she'll react when
she finds out that Diego's dead.

375
00:22:35,937 --> 00:22:37,439
Congressman, you have a visitor.

376
00:22:39,149 --> 00:22:42,152
I believe you have good news for me?

377
00:22:42,736 --> 00:22:43,779
Bad news, Congressman…

378
00:22:44,529 --> 00:22:47,949
Jaguar's men broke into
the station and rescued Diego

379
00:22:48,033 --> 00:22:49,076
from the hands of our men.

380
00:22:53,830 --> 00:22:56,249
Fine. You may go. Go!

381
00:22:57,626 --> 00:22:59,628
Bunch of nincompoops!

382
00:23:07,302 --> 00:23:08,553
[Diego groaning]

383
00:23:10,430 --> 00:23:12,099
[tense music playing]

384
00:23:30,075 --> 00:23:32,119
[groaning]

385
00:23:39,793 --> 00:23:41,503
[groaning]

386
00:23:44,172 --> 00:23:45,799
[breathing heavily]

387
00:23:49,594 --> 00:23:50,595
Jaguar.

388
00:23:52,806 --> 00:23:54,141
Who are you, Jaguar?

389
00:23:57,018 --> 00:23:58,395
Why are you helping me?

390
00:23:59,813 --> 00:24:01,690
Are you also an enemy of the Ardientes?

391
00:24:06,820 --> 00:24:07,904
I know…

392
00:24:10,073 --> 00:24:11,867
I know they're responsible for this.

393
00:24:15,787 --> 00:24:17,831
The minute I get out of here,

394
00:24:20,250 --> 00:24:21,960
I'll make them pay.

395
00:24:24,296 --> 00:24:25,755
They'll all pay.

396
00:24:39,561 --> 00:24:41,855
Well? How did it go? Where's Diego?

397
00:24:41,938 --> 00:24:45,609
As expected, the Ardientes
wanted to have him killed.

398
00:24:46,193 --> 00:24:49,613
It's a good thing we got there.
Otherwise, he'd be dead by now.

399
00:24:49,696 --> 00:24:52,449
Didn't I tell you to get him out of there?

400
00:24:52,532 --> 00:24:56,870
Jaguar, he refused to come. He says he's
innocent, so he doesn't need to escape.

401
00:24:57,621 --> 00:25:01,208
That stubborn kid
still puts his principles first.

402
00:25:02,083 --> 00:25:03,084
[sighs]

403
00:25:03,919 --> 00:25:06,046
Fine. Let's get ready.

404
00:25:06,129 --> 00:25:07,339
Why, Jaguar?

405
00:25:08,173 --> 00:25:10,175
It's time for Diego and I to work together

406
00:25:10,258 --> 00:25:12,135
and take the Ardientes down.

407
00:25:12,219 --> 00:25:15,180
[ominous music playing]

408
00:25:19,559 --> 00:25:21,102
-Is everything ready?
-Yes, doc.

409
00:25:21,186 --> 00:25:22,395
Good.

410
00:25:22,479 --> 00:25:23,605
[Diego groans]

411
00:25:25,440 --> 00:25:26,399
Sir…

412
00:25:26,483 --> 00:25:30,111
[soft piano music playing]

413
00:25:30,195 --> 00:25:31,279
[groans]

414
00:25:31,363 --> 00:25:34,115
We need to clean and treat your wounds.

415
00:25:35,367 --> 00:25:38,328
Nurse, have a portable
X-ray machine sent here

416
00:25:38,411 --> 00:25:39,704
to make sure that the patient is

417
00:25:39,788 --> 00:25:41,248
not suffering from any bone fractures.

418
00:25:41,331 --> 00:25:43,583
-Okay?
-Yes, doc. Excuse me.

419
00:25:43,667 --> 00:25:45,126
Have a seat.

420
00:25:50,048 --> 00:25:51,675
-Careful. Relax.
-[Diego groans]

421
00:25:54,427 --> 00:25:58,473
After I treat your wounds,
you can eat and get some rest.

422
00:26:02,435 --> 00:26:06,022
Tell Jaguar that I don't need his help.

423
00:26:10,277 --> 00:26:11,194
Wait.

424
00:26:12,112 --> 00:26:13,780
[brooding music playing]

425
00:26:17,826 --> 00:26:18,952
He wants to talk to you.

426
00:26:19,035 --> 00:26:20,745
[tense music playing]

427
00:26:27,627 --> 00:26:29,379
[Loring] Oh, Ma'am Camia.

428
00:26:29,713 --> 00:26:32,757
I have a bad feeling about
that judge's disappearance.

429
00:26:33,300 --> 00:26:35,552
What did you say, Loring? The judge…

430
00:26:35,635 --> 00:26:36,886
-Yes.
-[Pandoy] She's missing?

431
00:26:37,595 --> 00:26:41,266
Those damned Ardientes
will do everything to win!

432
00:26:42,017 --> 00:26:44,978
Yes, and I'm worried about Diego's case!

433
00:26:45,395 --> 00:26:48,523
Mr. Pandoy, Miss Loring, please calm down.

434
00:26:49,858 --> 00:26:50,984
Ma'am, it's just…

435
00:26:51,609 --> 00:26:55,363
It's hard to stay calm when you
know your child is in danger.

436
00:26:55,447 --> 00:26:56,990
[soft music playing]

437
00:26:58,074 --> 00:27:00,410
I know how you feel, Miss Loring.

438
00:27:01,077 --> 00:27:03,246
But, we must stay strong.

439
00:27:03,872 --> 00:27:07,042
We have to believe
that Diego will get past this.

440
00:27:07,834 --> 00:27:08,960
Ma'am, I know that.

441
00:27:09,044 --> 00:27:11,755
I believe that Diego can handle this.

442
00:27:12,339 --> 00:27:15,800
I just don't want him to get hurt.

443
00:27:16,217 --> 00:27:20,805
All his life, he's faced nothing
but pain from the Ardientes.

444
00:27:21,681 --> 00:27:24,642
Now, I just want him to be happy.

445
00:27:27,062 --> 00:27:31,191
Please have faith.
Diego will soon be free.

446
00:27:32,567 --> 00:27:34,694
Diego will be free from the Ardientes.

447
00:27:37,447 --> 00:27:39,115
[somber music playing]

448
00:27:44,913 --> 00:27:46,623
[ominous music playing]

449
00:28:04,933 --> 00:28:06,101
What do you want from me?

450
00:28:08,895 --> 00:28:10,105
Why are you helping me?

451
00:28:14,150 --> 00:28:16,069
No. This is not good.

452
00:28:17,195 --> 00:28:17,987
Okay?

453
00:28:18,822 --> 00:28:21,533
Jaguar is now Diego's protector
and supporter.

454
00:28:22,659 --> 00:28:24,035
He's now a legitimate threat.

455
00:28:25,161 --> 00:28:26,246
That he is.

456
00:28:26,955 --> 00:28:31,167
And that means
the fight will only get tougher.

457
00:28:32,627 --> 00:28:33,628
But…

458
00:28:34,921 --> 00:28:36,589
We are Ardientes.

459
00:28:37,632 --> 00:28:41,386
We've been through
a lot of battles and wars.

460
00:28:42,804 --> 00:28:48,935
As the battle draws out longer,
the fiercer we become.

461
00:28:50,729 --> 00:28:52,605
If they're looking for a good fight,

462
00:28:53,815 --> 00:28:54,941
we'll give them one.

463
00:28:58,027 --> 00:29:00,530
Been there, done that.

464
00:29:05,326 --> 00:29:06,995
[sinister music playing]

465
00:29:16,838 --> 00:29:19,424
Jaguar says, given your situation,

466
00:29:19,507 --> 00:29:20,967
you're the one who needs him.

467
00:29:22,427 --> 00:29:24,763
He's going to help you run for governor…

468
00:29:25,889 --> 00:29:29,851
by providing you with money,
personnel, and weapons.

469
00:29:31,102 --> 00:29:32,187
And, Diego,

470
00:29:32,604 --> 00:29:36,024
he also guarantees your victory
in your fight against Arnaldo.

471
00:29:37,108 --> 00:29:40,278
First of all, I don't trust
anyone who hides their face…

472
00:29:41,070 --> 00:29:42,614
and doesn't choose to talk.

473
00:29:42,697 --> 00:29:45,033
Second, I don't need your dirty money.

474
00:29:47,327 --> 00:29:48,328
Lastly…

475
00:29:49,454 --> 00:29:54,375
I'll defeat the Ardientes
using the force of the masses.

476
00:29:55,585 --> 00:29:57,754
What I want is change for Ardiente,

477
00:29:58,421 --> 00:30:02,592
not to replace a demon with another demon.

478
00:30:03,134 --> 00:30:04,761
[tense music playing]

479
00:30:38,545 --> 00:30:42,715
So… How do you want to go, Emilia?

480
00:30:43,424 --> 00:30:47,887
Do you want to get shot
and die right away?

481
00:30:48,805 --> 00:30:53,810
Or do you want it to be long and painful?

482
00:30:54,811 --> 00:30:56,855
Do you want to suffer before you die?

483
00:30:59,816 --> 00:31:01,276
Have you decided yet?

484
00:31:02,443 --> 00:31:03,486
Or…

485
00:31:04,821 --> 00:31:05,947
Better yet…

486
00:31:06,030 --> 00:31:07,907
[tense music playing]

487
00:31:10,076 --> 00:31:13,872
Should I flay you alive
and pour acid on you?

488
00:31:14,497 --> 00:31:15,790
Then, I'll burn you to death.

489
00:31:16,165 --> 00:31:20,336
Isn't that a grand entrance to hell?

490
00:31:21,170 --> 00:31:22,463
How do you like that?

491
00:31:22,881 --> 00:31:25,842
Are you sure you want
to end things this way?

492
00:31:27,302 --> 00:31:28,803
I'm warning you, Natalie.

493
00:31:30,805 --> 00:31:32,515
[tense music playing]

494
00:31:44,402 --> 00:31:46,112
<i>I need to get out of here.</i>

495
00:31:47,780 --> 00:31:49,240
[tense music playing]

496
00:31:57,749 --> 00:31:59,417
[ominous music playing]

497
00:31:59,876 --> 00:32:03,004
You don't call the shots anymore!

498
00:32:04,130 --> 00:32:05,256
I do.

499
00:32:06,674 --> 00:32:08,051
That one's for my dad.

500
00:32:11,220 --> 00:32:12,221
[mocking tone] More.

501
00:32:16,726 --> 00:32:20,772
And that one's for the wound in his chest.

502
00:32:22,774 --> 00:32:24,484
[ominous music playing]

503
00:32:26,778 --> 00:32:29,113
[Natalie grunting]

504
00:32:30,573 --> 00:32:32,283
Are you done? Then, it's my turn.

505
00:32:32,367 --> 00:32:34,285
Go reunite with your father in hell!

506
00:32:35,828 --> 00:32:36,996
[goons] Ma'am! Ma'am! Ma'am! Ma'am!

507
00:32:37,622 --> 00:32:40,166
Sit down, bitch.

508
00:32:41,751 --> 00:32:43,419
That's right.

509
00:32:47,590 --> 00:32:52,095
I won't let you go until you die, Emilia.

510
00:32:53,930 --> 00:32:56,557
You murdered my father.

511
00:32:57,266 --> 00:32:58,810
So I have to do the same to you.

512
00:32:59,519 --> 00:33:02,981
That's right, bitch. Sit down.

513
00:33:03,773 --> 00:33:05,441
[tense music playing]

514
00:33:17,662 --> 00:33:19,330
[tense music playing]

515
00:33:40,476 --> 00:33:41,352
Boys.

516
00:33:42,937 --> 00:33:44,689
[foreboding music playing]

517
00:33:49,861 --> 00:33:53,156
The next time this woman tries to escape…

518
00:33:55,908 --> 00:33:58,578
I'll shoot every bullet
in this gun into your brains!

519
00:33:59,287 --> 00:34:00,288
You got it?

520
00:34:01,664 --> 00:34:03,291
Don't be stupid!

521
00:34:03,374 --> 00:34:04,542
Understand?!

522
00:34:09,172 --> 00:34:10,798
Your son really is stubborn.

523
00:34:11,716 --> 00:34:14,469
Let's see how much he can take.

524
00:34:15,678 --> 00:34:17,722
I know Diego. I'm his dad.

525
00:34:19,474 --> 00:34:21,809
If his loved ones are in danger…

526
00:34:22,685 --> 00:34:24,645
he'll have no choice but to give in.

527
00:34:25,271 --> 00:34:26,522
He'll bite the bullet.

528
00:34:27,857 --> 00:34:29,984
Jaguar, can you do that to your own son?

529
00:34:31,611 --> 00:34:33,029
If that's what it takes

530
00:34:33,112 --> 00:34:35,531
to make him win against Arnaldo, why not?

531
00:34:38,951 --> 00:34:40,244
Now, where was I?

532
00:34:42,080 --> 00:34:45,083
Oh yeah. You know what?

533
00:34:45,750 --> 00:34:48,377
Even if we both have our differences,

534
00:34:49,420 --> 00:34:50,755
I still have a heart.

535
00:34:51,881 --> 00:34:53,800
That's why I'm giving you a chance

536
00:34:54,425 --> 00:34:58,930
to talk to someone very special.

537
00:35:02,058 --> 00:35:04,811
And the question is,

538
00:35:06,813 --> 00:35:07,980
who could it be?!

539
00:35:08,439 --> 00:35:09,941
[suspenseful music]

540
00:35:11,067 --> 00:35:15,279
Letter A, is it your father, Julio?

541
00:35:16,322 --> 00:35:19,158
Or letter B,

542
00:35:20,368 --> 00:35:23,496
your son, Mayor Arnaldo?

543
00:35:23,996 --> 00:35:27,917
Or letter C…

544
00:35:29,585 --> 00:35:33,798
your beloved husband, Raul?

545
00:35:35,133 --> 00:35:36,843
I wonder…

546
00:35:39,846 --> 00:35:41,639
Why do I have his number?

547
00:35:46,769 --> 00:35:48,020
[phone ringing]

548
00:35:51,315 --> 00:35:52,692
[phone ringing]

549
00:35:54,402 --> 00:35:56,195
-Hello?
-Hello, Raul.

550
00:35:56,571 --> 00:35:57,780
Emilia?

551
00:35:58,531 --> 00:36:01,576
Save me because Natalie
is going to kill me.

552
00:36:01,659 --> 00:36:03,035
Save me now!

553
00:36:03,119 --> 00:36:04,620
[laughing]

554
00:36:06,330 --> 00:36:07,915
Emilia. Hello?

555
00:36:07,999 --> 00:36:09,417
Hi, Raul!

556
00:36:11,085 --> 00:36:13,004
[giggles] Did you miss me?

557
00:36:13,713 --> 00:36:15,756
Did you hear what your wife said?

558
00:36:16,215 --> 00:36:17,633
<i>She said…</i>

559
00:36:17,717 --> 00:36:21,596
you should save her from me!

560
00:36:22,805 --> 00:36:24,974
Natalie, what are you gonna do to Emilia?!

561
00:36:25,057 --> 00:36:26,893
Natalie, don't hurt her!

562
00:36:32,815 --> 00:36:35,776
Natalie?! Hello! Natalie!

563
00:36:36,652 --> 00:36:38,738
[tense music playing]

564
00:36:40,823 --> 00:36:42,491
Rufo, we have a problem.

565
00:36:42,575 --> 00:36:44,118
Natalie has taken Emilia!

566
00:36:44,202 --> 00:36:46,871
Don't let her hurt Emilia!

567
00:36:50,750 --> 00:36:51,667
[grunts]

568
00:36:54,045 --> 00:36:56,047
[suspenseful music playing]

569
00:36:58,049 --> 00:36:59,300
[sighs]

570
00:37:00,343 --> 00:37:05,598
For some reason, your husband
told me not to kill you.

571
00:37:07,016 --> 00:37:10,519
Now, why would I listen to him?
Why should I do what he says?

572
00:37:11,354 --> 00:37:15,691
It's not as if I'm sleeping
with your husband.

573
00:37:16,984 --> 00:37:20,446
Oh, yeah! [chuckles] I am!

574
00:37:20,905 --> 00:37:21,697
[Natalie laughs]

575
00:37:21,781 --> 00:37:24,617
My husband would never sleep with you.

576
00:37:24,700 --> 00:37:27,036
You sure about that, Emilia?

577
00:37:27,119 --> 00:37:28,621
[Natalie laughing]

578
00:37:29,163 --> 00:37:30,706
I wouldn't say so.

579
00:37:31,332 --> 00:37:34,377
You know what? You're looking at me.

580
00:37:34,877 --> 00:37:37,004
And you know I'm sexy.

581
00:37:37,088 --> 00:37:40,424
You, of all people, know…

582
00:37:40,925 --> 00:37:46,013
-that men love me.
-You aren't his type!

583
00:37:47,181 --> 00:37:48,808
I know my husband better.

584
00:37:48,891 --> 00:37:53,187
He wouldn't go after
some cheap slut like you!

585
00:37:53,271 --> 00:37:54,272
Cheap?

586
00:37:55,606 --> 00:37:57,817
Me?! [laughs]

587
00:37:58,317 --> 00:37:59,402
Don't worry about that.

588
00:38:00,695 --> 00:38:05,783
When you die,
I'll look after your husband.

589
00:38:05,866 --> 00:38:08,995
And guess what? I'm gonna
take good care of him.

590
00:38:09,745 --> 00:38:11,038
Who are you calling "cheap" again?

591
00:38:11,706 --> 00:38:13,374
Is it me or you?

592
00:38:26,846 --> 00:38:29,348
[action music playing]

593
00:38:36,188 --> 00:38:37,732
[Ivy grunting]

594
00:38:57,585 --> 00:38:59,253
[action music playing]

595
00:39:02,590 --> 00:39:04,091
My husband loves me.

596
00:39:04,175 --> 00:39:06,635
He even promised me
he wouldn't hurt me again.

597
00:39:06,719 --> 00:39:09,096
I'm sure you're just telling me
that to hurt me!

598
00:39:09,180 --> 00:39:11,057
-You're a liar!
-[laughs]

599
00:39:11,140 --> 00:39:15,186
You know that I'm not a liar!

600
00:39:16,395 --> 00:39:19,523
We were friends before. You know that.

601
00:39:21,484 --> 00:39:23,235
[sighs heavily] Did I hurt you?

602
00:39:24,904 --> 00:39:26,030
Yeah.

603
00:39:26,113 --> 00:39:30,284
I pity you, Emilia. You're miserable.

604
00:39:31,410 --> 00:39:35,164
Raul, for some reason, is your life.

605
00:39:35,581 --> 00:39:38,793
No matter what he does,
even if he cheats on you,

606
00:39:39,251 --> 00:39:40,544
you will always be there for him.

607
00:39:41,295 --> 00:39:47,718
But it doesn't matter anymore
because you'll die soon.

608
00:39:48,677 --> 00:39:50,346
[tense music playing]

609
00:39:53,349 --> 00:39:54,809
[Emilia chuckling]

610
00:39:56,644 --> 00:39:57,770
Find it funny?

611
00:39:58,896 --> 00:40:00,981
My husband loves me.

612
00:40:02,358 --> 00:40:03,275
How about you?

613
00:40:04,693 --> 00:40:06,153
You're just a wet pillow.

614
00:40:07,154 --> 00:40:10,574
[ominous music playing]

615
00:40:16,789 --> 00:40:19,834
[somber music playing]

616
00:40:23,379 --> 00:40:24,880
[jail cell opening]

617
00:40:28,175 --> 00:40:29,468
[cell door squeaking]

618
00:40:45,568 --> 00:40:50,865
[tense music playing]

619
00:40:57,997 --> 00:40:58,998
Right here.

620
00:41:00,541 --> 00:41:04,712
I've prepared this spot
just for you, Emilia.

621
00:41:09,383 --> 00:41:10,509
You know…

622
00:41:11,802 --> 00:41:13,846
I've been waiting for this moment.

623
00:41:15,806 --> 00:41:17,558
What were you saying again?

624
00:41:18,058 --> 00:41:20,186
Raul loves you?

625
00:41:21,687 --> 00:41:22,813
Are you sure about that?

626
00:41:23,481 --> 00:41:26,942
[ominous music playing]

627
00:41:27,234 --> 00:41:28,694
Because the only thing

628
00:41:28,777 --> 00:41:30,613
that's in love with you right now…

629
00:41:31,739 --> 00:41:33,324
is my little friend.

630
00:41:34,783 --> 00:41:38,204
I've waited for this moment, Emilia.

631
00:41:39,163 --> 00:41:40,331
[sniffles]

632
00:41:40,414 --> 00:41:41,373
[exhales]

633
00:41:41,457 --> 00:41:43,501
[tense music playing]

634
00:41:54,720 --> 00:41:56,263
[tense music playing]

635
00:41:58,682 --> 00:42:01,519
This feels really good right now.

636
00:42:03,938 --> 00:42:08,400
There's a grand reunion just for you.

637
00:42:10,611 --> 00:42:12,404
Bye, Emilia.

638
00:42:13,739 --> 00:42:15,407
[tense music playing]

639
00:42:22,498 --> 00:42:27,795
<i>You do deserve this for</i>
<i>everything you've done, Emilia.</i>

640
00:42:33,259 --> 00:42:35,970
[tense music playing]

641
00:42:39,682 --> 00:42:41,267
-[Natalie shouts]
-[gunshot]

642
00:42:49,400 --> 00:42:51,485
What's wrong with you?!

643
00:42:52,486 --> 00:42:53,612
Jaguar?!

644
00:42:55,531 --> 00:42:56,532
Keep an eye on her!

645
00:42:57,575 --> 00:43:00,286
[tense music playing]

646
00:43:03,080 --> 00:43:04,707
[action music playing]

647
00:43:11,630 --> 00:43:12,548
Ivy!

648
00:43:14,592 --> 00:43:16,677
I was supposed to leave you to die here

649
00:43:16,760 --> 00:43:19,430
because you wanted Natalie to kill me.

650
00:43:19,847 --> 00:43:22,600
But then, I'd never do that
to Arnaldo. He might assume

651
00:43:22,683 --> 00:43:24,810
that I let my future
mother-in-law die here.

652
00:43:25,352 --> 00:43:26,895
[Emilia sobbing]

653
00:43:26,979 --> 00:43:28,814
Ivy, thank you.

654
00:43:30,065 --> 00:43:34,445
<i>This isn't how I envisioned</i>
<i>your death, Emilia.</i>

655
00:43:37,239 --> 00:43:38,449
Ivy, thank you!

656
00:43:38,824 --> 00:43:39,742
[scoffs]

657
00:43:39,825 --> 00:43:40,909
Don't thank me just yet.

658
00:43:40,993 --> 00:43:42,453
We need to get out of here first.

659
00:43:44,538 --> 00:43:46,582
-Run, Emilia!
-Ivy, wait!

660
00:43:46,665 --> 00:43:48,500
Do you want to die? Hurry up!

661
00:43:49,001 --> 00:43:50,878
-Come here.
-Let go of me!

662
00:43:51,795 --> 00:43:53,505
Natalie, what do you think you're doing?!

663
00:43:53,839 --> 00:43:57,760
Have you forgotten already?
She killed my father!

664
00:43:58,677 --> 00:44:00,429
Of course, I have to avenge him.

665
00:44:00,929 --> 00:44:03,223
I know all that,
but we can still use Emilia!

666
00:44:03,599 --> 00:44:04,808
For what?!

667
00:44:06,352 --> 00:44:07,353
Tell me!

668
00:44:08,771 --> 00:44:12,024
I had Emilia's wake scheduled
today so I have to kill her!

669
00:44:12,358 --> 00:44:14,568
No one can stop me! Not even you!

670
00:44:14,860 --> 00:44:18,739
Don't you ever test me.
I don't want my plans ruined.

671
00:44:18,822 --> 00:44:20,074
So you better release Emilia!

672
00:44:23,911 --> 00:44:25,579
[tense music playing]

673
00:44:42,304 --> 00:44:44,765
-[sighs]
-[somber music playing]

674
00:44:50,854 --> 00:44:52,731
[voice prompt] <i>The subscriber</i>
<i>cannot be reached.</i>

675
00:44:52,815 --> 00:44:54,441
<i>Please try again later.</i>

676
00:44:58,320 --> 00:45:00,864
Lily, you haven't contacted me
for almost a day.

677
00:45:01,573 --> 00:45:03,158
Where on earth are you?

678
00:45:10,916 --> 00:45:12,251
[Arnaldo] You know what, Grandpa?

679
00:45:13,168 --> 00:45:14,169
I was just thinking.

680
00:45:16,964 --> 00:45:18,006
What if…

681
00:45:19,675 --> 00:45:21,635
my dad is the Jaguar?

682
00:45:22,177 --> 00:45:24,888
[laughing]

683
00:45:25,848 --> 00:45:27,015
What?

684
00:45:27,099 --> 00:45:29,685
That is the most
ridiculous thing I can think of.

685
00:45:31,145 --> 00:45:33,230
Your father is poorer than a rat.

686
00:45:33,647 --> 00:45:38,777
I mean, he still has to ask me
for money to buy underwear.

687
00:45:39,987 --> 00:45:44,116
And you would think that
he can be someone like Jaguar?

688
00:45:44,450 --> 00:45:45,742
[laughing]

689
00:45:47,161 --> 00:45:49,079
But this Jaguar…

690
00:45:50,164 --> 00:45:51,874
I'm certain he's rich.

691
00:45:53,500 --> 00:45:56,378
And I have a feeling that he's connected

692
00:45:56,462 --> 00:45:58,005
to a lot of powerful people.

693
00:46:01,258 --> 00:46:05,888
I really wonder who he is.

694
00:46:07,723 --> 00:46:08,932
Why--

695
00:46:09,016 --> 00:46:11,560
Why has he only appeared now?

696
00:46:13,187 --> 00:46:14,062
[phone ringing]

697
00:46:16,315 --> 00:46:17,441
[phone ringing]

698
00:46:17,524 --> 00:46:18,525
[Julio chuckles]

699
00:46:19,776 --> 00:46:21,028
-Oh!
-[phone ringing]

700
00:46:21,111 --> 00:46:22,404
Speak of the devil.

701
00:46:23,614 --> 00:46:26,033
It's your dad, the rodent.

702
00:46:29,411 --> 00:46:30,245
Hello, Raul.

703
00:46:30,329 --> 00:46:31,205
Yes, Papa.

704
00:46:31,288 --> 00:46:34,541
This better be worth my time, or else…

705
00:46:34,625 --> 00:46:38,295
Papa, Emilia called me asking for help.

706
00:46:38,795 --> 00:46:40,672
<i>She and Ivy were kidnapped.</i>

707
00:46:40,756 --> 00:46:42,174
She said they were going to be killed.

708
00:46:42,257 --> 00:46:43,175
What?!

709
00:46:45,761 --> 00:46:49,556
That bastard Jaguar is really
making my blood boil!

710
00:46:49,640 --> 00:46:51,225
He's obviously challenging me!

711
00:46:51,308 --> 00:46:52,518
Why? What happened?

712
00:46:52,601 --> 00:46:55,729
He kidnapped your mother and Ivy.

713
00:46:55,896 --> 00:46:58,440
What?! We have to save them!

714
00:46:58,524 --> 00:47:03,987
Hello, Dad. What did Mom say?
How's Ivy? Is she hurt?

715
00:47:04,071 --> 00:47:06,406
I don't know, son.
The line got disconnected.

716
00:47:06,990 --> 00:47:08,283
How about this, Arnaldo?

717
00:47:08,367 --> 00:47:09,910
Let's help each other look for them.

718
00:47:12,913 --> 00:47:15,916
Jaguar is really getting on my nerves.

719
00:47:19,002 --> 00:47:21,547
[tense music playing]

720
00:47:24,716 --> 00:47:27,469
[Camia] <i>Even though Diego's in prison,</i>
<i>we can beat them together.</i>

721
00:47:27,553 --> 00:47:29,012
[Emilia] <i>We should look for a place</i>

722
00:47:29,096 --> 00:47:30,556
<i>without trash lying around.</i>

723
00:47:30,639 --> 00:47:31,807
<i>You're garbage!</i>

724
00:47:31,890 --> 00:47:32,683
<i>Shut up!</i>

725
00:47:32,766 --> 00:47:35,269
<i>You won't be able to salvage</i>
<i>your tarnished reputation.</i>

726
00:47:35,352 --> 00:47:37,145
<i>Because we will win this election!</i>

727
00:47:37,521 --> 00:47:39,189
<i>Is he working with Jaguar?</i>

728
00:47:39,273 --> 00:47:43,193
<i>if they continue to work</i>
<i>together, I might lose.</i>

729
00:47:43,277 --> 00:47:44,778
<i>"Call me, my beautiful."</i>

730
00:47:44,861 --> 00:47:46,613
<i>Jaguar's quite the sweet-talker, isn't he?</i>

731
00:47:46,697 --> 00:47:48,949
<i>-Just like Raul?</i>
<i>-If you really want me,</i>

732
00:47:49,032 --> 00:47:50,158
<i>then show yourself.</i>

733
00:47:50,242 --> 00:47:52,035
<i>You can't hide under your mask forever.</i>

734
00:47:52,119 --> 00:47:53,287
[Jaguar] <i>I have one condition.</i>

735
00:47:53,370 --> 00:47:55,247
<i>I want it to be just the two of us.</i>

736
00:47:55,330 --> 00:47:56,206
<i>No one else.</i>

737
00:47:56,957 --> 00:48:00,669
[theme music playing]
